Subject: [PATCH 01/61] LPM.ratio/UPM.ratio/Co.*/D.*/PM.matrix: honour integer
 targets

The C++ wrappers accepted a target only when is<NumericVector>(target)
was true, which is FALSE for an integer vector. An integer target such
as 2L, 1:3 or sort() of an integer variable was silently replaced by
mean(variable) (colMeans for PM.matrix). NNS.CDF passes sort(variable),
so the CDF of any integer vector was a single constant.

Accept integer vectors as supplied targets (coerced to double), as LPM()
and UPM() already do through as.numeric().

Evidence (x = c(1,2,3,10)), before -> after:
  LPM.ratio(0, 2L, x)              0.75       -> 0.5 (= LPM.ratio(0, 2, x))
  LPM.ratio(0, 1:3, x)             0.75       -> 0.25 0.5 0.75
  Co.LPM(1, x, x, 2L, 2L)          3.5        -> 0.25
  D.LPM(1, 1, x, rev(x), 0L, 0L)   4.5        -> 0
  PM.matrix(1,1,c(0L,0L),A)$cupm   0          -> 8
  NNS.CDF(1:10)$Function$CDF       0.5 x 10   -> 0.1 0.2 ... 1.0
  NNS.CDF(rpois(200,3))            0.645 only -> 9-step ECDF

Results change only for integer-typed targets, which were wrong.
---
 src/partial_moments_rcpp.cpp | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/partial_moments_rcpp.cpp b/src/partial_moments_rcpp.cpp
index e8fbf54..1d00cc5 100644
--- a/src/partial_moments_rcpp.cpp
+++ b/src/partial_moments_rcpp.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,14 @@ static inline bool isInteger(double value) {
   return value == static_cast<int>(value);
 }
 
+// A user-supplied target is any non-NULL numeric (double or integer) vector.
+// Integer targets (e.g. 2L, 1:3, or sort() of an integer variable) must be
+// used as given, not silently replaced by mean(variable).
+static inline bool is_supplied_target(const RObject &target) {
+  return !target.isNULL() &&
+    (is<NumericVector>(target) || is<IntegerVector>(target));
+}
